---
title: "Gil Goals"
layout: layouts/ffBase.njk
permalink: /shrines/finalfantasyxiv/gil/
description: "Aggro Phobic's road to the gil cap — savings milestones, ridiculous collectible purchases and the Frog Treasury."
customcss: "/assets/css/ffxiv/gil.css"
---

{% set g = ffxivGil %}
{% set s = ffxivGilShopping %}

<div class="ff-gil">
  <section class="ff-gil-hero ff-card">
    <div class="ff-gil-hero__copy">
      <p class="ff-gil-kicker">◇ the frog treasury ◇</p>
      <h1>Gil Goals</h1>
      <p>
        Aggro Phobic’s slow march toward completely unreasonable wealth —
        while still spending gil on mounts, minions, orchestrion rolls and
        anything else shiny enough to ruin the savings plan.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="ff-gil-coin-stack" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="ff-gil-coin ff-gil-coin--one">◇</span>
      <span class="ff-gil-coin ff-gil-coin--two">◇</span>
      <span class="ff-gil-coin ff-gil-coin--three">◇</span>
      <b>✦</b>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ff-gil-vault ff-card">
    <div class="ff-gil-vault__main">
      <p class="ff-gil-kicker">current fortune</p>

      {% if g.currentGil > 0 %}
        <p class="ff-gil-vault__number">{{ g.currentGilDisplay }}</p>
        <p class="ff-gil-vault__percent">{{ g.capPercentDisplay }} of the gil cap</p>
      {% else %}
        <p class="ff-gil-vault__number ff-gil-vault__number--empty">add current gil</p>
        <p class="ff-gil-vault__percent">
          Set <code>currentGil</code> once in <code>ffxivGil.js</code>.
        </p>
      {% endif %}

      <div
        class="ff-gil-progress"
        role="progressbar"
        aria-label="Progress toward gil cap"
        aria-valuemin="0"
        aria-valuemax="{{ g.cap }}"
        aria-valuenow="{{ g.currentGil }}"
      >
        <span style="width: {{ g.capPercent }}%"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="ff-gil-vault__capline">
        <span>0</span>
        <strong>♡ someday: {{ g.capDisplay }}</strong>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="ff-gil-next">
      <span class="ff-gil-next__spark" aria-hidden="true">✦</span>
      <p class="ff-gil-kicker">next savings milestone</p>
      <strong>{{ g.nextMilestone.display }}</strong>

      {% if g.currentGil > 0 %}
        <p>{{ g.nextMilestone.deltaDisplay }} to go</p>

        <div
          class="ff-gil-progress ff-gil-progress--milestone"
          role="progressbar"
          aria-label="Progress toward next milestone"
          aria-valuemin="0"
          aria-valuemax="100"
          aria-valuenow="{{ g.nextMilestone.bandPercent }}"
        >
          <span style="width: {{ g.nextMilestone.bandPercent }}%"></span>
        </div>
      {% else %}
        <p>Your first little target is waiting.</p>
      {% endif %}
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="ff-gil-stats">
    <article class="ff-gil-stat ff-card">
      <span aria-hidden="true">◇</span>
      <small>liquid gil</small>
      <strong>{{ g.currentGilDisplay }}</strong>
      <p>What Aggro can actually see in the purse right now.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="ff-gil-stat ff-card">
      <span aria-hidden="true">♡</span>
      <small>collector spending</small>
      <strong>{{ g.trackedCollectionSpendDisplay }}</strong>
      <p>Tracked purchases that became permanent collection progress.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="ff-gil-stat ff-card">
      <span aria-hidden="true">✦</span>
      <small>lifetime progress</small>
      <strong>{{ g.lifetimeProgressDisplay }}</strong>
      <p>Current gil + tracked collector spending, so buying things still counts.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="ff-gil-stat ff-card">
      <span aria-hidden="true">♜</span>
      <small>do-not-touch floor</small>
      <strong>{{ g.gilFloorDisplay }}</strong>
      <p>{{ g.safeSpendDisplay }} is currently above the safety floor.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="ff-gil-road ff-card">
    <div class="ff-gil-section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="ff-gil-kicker">✦ road to one billion</p>
        <h2>The increasingly silly milestones</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The cap stays the mountain in the distance; these are the little flags
        that make getting there actually feel like progress.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="ff-gil-road__track">
      {% for milestone in g.milestones %}
        <div class="ff-gil-mile{% if milestone.reached %} is-reached{% endif %}{% if milestone.isNext %} is-next{% endif %}">
          <span class="ff-gil-mile__dot" aria-hidden="true">
            {% if milestone.reached %}✓{% elif milestone.isNext %}♡{% else %}◇{% endif %}
          </span>
          <strong>{{ milestone.label }}</strong>
          {% if milestone.isNext %}
            <small>next</small>
          {% elif milestone.reached %}
            <small>reached</small>
          {% else %}
            <small>later</small>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <p class="ff-gil-road__scribble">
      tiny Eorzean oligarch in training ♡
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="ff-gil-collector ff-card">
    <div class="ff-gil-section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="ff-gil-kicker">♡ collector fund</p>
        <h2>Turning gil into permanent nonsense</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Spending doesn't erase the journey here. Once a collectible is bought,
        its price moves into Collector Spending instead.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="ff-gil-collector-grid">
      <article class="ff-gil-collection-card ff-gil-collection-card--mounts">
        <header>
          <span class="ff-gil-collection-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">♞</span>
          <div>
            <small>the ridiculous gold mount fund</small>
            <h3>Luxury mounts</h3>
          </div>
        </header>

        <div class="ff-gil-collection-card__big">
          <strong>{{ g.luxuryMount.owned }} / {{ g.luxuryMount.total }}</strong>
          <span>{{ g.luxuryMount.spentDisplay }} / {{ g.luxuryMount.totalCostDisplay }}</span>
        </div>

        <div class="ff-gil-progress ff-gil-progress--collector">
          <span style="width: {{ g.luxuryMount.percent }}%"></span>
        </div>

        <p class="ff-gil-collection-card__remaining">
          {{ g.luxuryMount.remainingDisplay }} of fixed vendor purchases remaining.
        </p>

        <div class="ff-gil-shopping-list">
          {% for mount in g.luxuryMounts %}
            <div class="ff-gil-shopping-item{% if mount.owned %} is-owned{% endif %}">
              <span class="ff-gil-shopping-item__check" aria-hidden="true">
                {% if mount.owned %}✓{% else %}◇{% endif %}
              </span>

              <div>
                <strong>{{ mount.name }}</strong>
                <small>{{ mount.source }}</small>
              </div>

              <span class="ff-gil-shopping-item__price">{{ mount.costCompact }}</span>
            </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>

        {% if g.luxuryMount.next %}
          <div class="ff-gil-next-buy">
            <small>next unowned target</small>
            <strong>{{ g.luxuryMount.next.name }}</strong>

            {% if g.currentGil <= 0 %}
              <span>Add current gil to see affordability.</span>
            {% elif g.luxuryMount.next.canAffordSafely %}
              <span class="is-good">Affordable without breaking the gil floor ♡</span>
            {% elif g.luxuryMount.next.canAffordRaw %}
              <span class="is-warn">Technically affordable, but it would break the gil floor.</span>
            {% else %}
              <span>{{ g.luxuryMount.next.shortByDisplay }} short.</span>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
        {% endif %}
      </article>

      <article class="ff-gil-collection-card">
        <header>
          <span class="ff-gil-collection-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">♧</span>
          <div>
            <small>little creatures, big shopping list</small>
            <h3>Minions</h3>
          </div>
        </header>

        {% if s.ok %}
          <div class="ff-gil-collection-card__big">
            <strong>{{ s.minions.ownedBuyableCount }} / {{ s.minions.buyableCount }}</strong>
            <span>gil-buyable minions owned</span>
          </div>

          <div class="ff-gil-progress ff-gil-progress--collector">
            <span style="width: {{ s.minions.completionPercent }}%"></span>
          </div>

          <p class="ff-gil-collection-card__remaining">
            {{ s.minions.missingCount }} gil-buyable minions still on Aggro’s shopping list.
          </p>

          <div class="ff-gil-mini-budget">
            <div>
              <small>fixed vendor buys left</small>
              <strong>{{ s.minions.vendor.totalDisplay }}</strong>
            </div>
            <div>
              <small>Lich marketboard estimate</small>
              <strong>{{ s.minions.market.estimateDisplay }}</strong>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="ff-gil-collection-card__note">
            Ownership is checked against Aggro’s public Lodestone collection.
            The full missing vendor + Market Board list is ready below.
          </p>
        {% else %}
          <div class="ff-gil-emptybar"><span>shopping data unavailable this build</span></div>
          <p class="ff-gil-collection-card__note">
            The minion card will repopulate automatically when the shopping-data refresh succeeds.
          </p>
        {% endif %}
      </article>

      <article class="ff-gil-collection-card">
        <header>
          <span class="ff-gil-collection-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">♫</span>
          <div>
            <small>expensive background music</small>
            <h3>Orchestrion rolls</h3>
          </div>
        </header>

        {% if s.ok %}
          {% if s.orchestrions.ownershipKnown %}
            <div class="ff-gil-collection-card__big">
              <strong>{{ s.orchestrions.ownedBuyableCount }} / {{ s.orchestrions.buyableCount }}</strong>
              <span>gil-buyable rolls owned</span>
            </div>

            <div class="ff-gil-progress ff-gil-progress--collector">
              <span style="width: {{ s.orchestrions.completionPercent }}%"></span>
            </div>

            <p class="ff-gil-collection-card__remaining">
              {{ s.orchestrions.missingCount }} gil-buyable rolls still missing.
            </p>
          {% else %}
            <div class="ff-gil-collection-card__big">
              <strong>{{ s.orchestrions.buyableCount }}</strong>
              <span>gil-buyable rolls in the catalogue</span>
            </div>

            <div class="ff-gil-emptybar">
              <span>ready for Aggro’s owned-roll import</span>
            </div>

            <p class="ff-gil-collection-card__remaining">
              The shopping catalogue is live; only Aggro’s owned orchestrions need importing.
            </p>
          {% endif %}

          <div class="ff-gil-mini-budget">
            <div>
              <small>fixed vendor catalogue</small>
              <strong>{{ s.orchestrions.vendor.totalDisplay }}</strong>
            </div>
            <div>
              <small>Lich marketboard catalogue</small>
              <strong>{{ s.orchestrions.market.estimateDisplay }}</strong>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="ff-gil-collection-card__note">
            Upload or paste Aggro’s owned orchestrion list when you have it and
            this card will switch to true owned / missing progress automatically.
            The full purchasable catalogue is already listed below.
          </p>
        {% else %}
          <div class="ff-gil-emptybar"><span>shopping data unavailable this build</span></div>
          <p class="ff-gil-collection-card__note">
            The orchestrion catalogue will repopulate automatically when the shopping-data refresh succeeds.
          </p>
        {% endif %}
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="ff-gil-shopping ff-card">
    <div class="ff-gil-section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="ff-gil-kicker">✦ actual shopping list</p>
        <h2>Everything Aggro can throw gil at</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Fixed-price vendor buys are exact. Marketboard prices are live-ish Lich
        estimates and will wiggle around between builds.
      </p>
    </div>

    {% if not s.ok %}
      <div class="ff-gil-shopping-error">
        <strong>Shopping data could not refresh this build.</strong>
        <p>{{ s.error }}</p>
      </div>
    {% else %}
      <div class="ff-gil-shopping-summary">
        <article>
          <small>missing buyables</small>
          <strong>{{ s.totals.missing }}</strong>
          <p>Across mounts, minions and orchestrion rolls.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <small>fixed vendor bill</small>
          <strong>{{ s.totals.vendorDisplay }}</strong>
          <p>Exact gil prices from purchase sources.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <small>Lich market estimate</small>
          <strong>{{ s.totals.marketEstimateDisplay }}</strong>
          <p>
            {% if s.totals.marketUnknownCount %}
              {{ s.totals.marketUnknownCount }} items currently have no usable listing.
            {% else %}
              All currently-priced market items included.
            {% endif %}
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <small>shopping mountain</small>
          <strong>{{ s.totals.combinedEstimateDisplay }}</strong>
          <p>Vendor total + currently available market estimates.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="ff-gil-shopping-toolbar">
        <label>
          <span>Find something</span>
          <input
            type="search"
            placeholder="search mounts, minions, songs…"
            data-gil-shopping-search
          >
        </label>

        <p>
          ♡ Mounts + minions auto-check against Aggro’s Lodestone.
          Orchestrions use the tiny owned list in the config file.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="ff-gil-shopping-categories">
        {% for category in s.categories %}
          <article class="ff-gil-shop-category">
            <header class="ff-gil-shop-category__head">
              <span class="ff-gil-shop-category__icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ category.icon }}</span>

              <div>
                <p class="ff-gil-kicker">
                  {% if category.ownershipMode == "lodestone" %}
                    Aggro ownership synced
                  {% elif category.ownershipMode == "manual" %}
                    manual owned list
                  {% else %}
                    ownership check unavailable
                  {% endif %}
                </p>
                <h3>{{ category.title }}</h3>
              </div>

              <div class="ff-gil-shop-category__counts">
                <strong>{{ category.missingCount }}</strong>
                <small>missing buyables</small>
              </div>
            </header>

            <div class="ff-gil-shop-category__stats">
              <div>
                <small>Fixed vendor</small>
                <strong>{{ category.vendor.count }}</strong>
                <span>{{ category.vendor.totalDisplay }}</span>
              </div>

              <div>
                <small>Marketboard</small>
                <strong>{{ category.market.count }}</strong>
                <span>{{ category.market.estimateDisplay }}</span>
              </div>

              <div>
                <small>Buyable owned</small>
                <strong>{{ category.ownedBuyableCount }} / {{ category.buyableCount }}</strong>
                <span>{{ category.completionPercent }}%</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <details class="ff-gil-shop-details" {% if loop.first %}open{% endif %}>
              <summary>
                <span>Fixed-price vendor purchases</span>
                <strong>{{ category.vendor.count }} · {{ category.vendor.totalDisplay }}</strong>
              </summary>

              {% if category.vendor.items.length %}
                <div class="ff-gil-shop-list">
                  {% for item in category.vendor.items %}
                    <div
                      class="ff-gil-shop-row"
                      data-gil-shopping-row
                      data-gil-shopping-name="{{ item.name | lower }}"
                    >
                      <span class="ff-gil-shop-row__mark" aria-hidden="true">◇</span>
                      <div class="ff-gil-shop-row__name">
                        <strong>{{ item.name }}</strong>
                        <small>{{ item.vendorSource or "Vendor purchase" }}</small>
                      </div>
                      <span class="ff-gil-shop-row__price">{{ item.vendorPriceDisplay }}</span>
                    </div>
                  {% endfor %}
                </div>
              {% else %}
                <p class="ff-gil-shop-empty">No missing fixed-price vendor purchases found.</p>
              {% endif %}
            </details>

            <details class="ff-gil-shop-details">
              <summary>
                <span>Marketboard shopping</span>
                <strong>{{ category.market.count }} · {{ category.market.estimateDisplay }}</strong>
              </summary>

              {% if category.market.items.length %}
                <div class="ff-gil-shop-list">
                  {% for item in category.market.items %}
                    <div
                      class="ff-gil-shop-row"
                      data-gil-shopping-row
                      data-gil-shopping-name="{{ item.name | lower }}"
                    >
                      <span class="ff-gil-shop-row__mark" aria-hidden="true">◇</span>
                      <div class="ff-gil-shop-row__name">
                        <strong>{{ item.name }}</strong>
                        <small>
                          Marketboard{% if item.patch %} · patch {{ item.patch }}{% endif %}
                        </small>
                      </div>
                      <span class="ff-gil-shop-row__price">
                        {{ item.marketPriceDisplay }}
                      </span>
                    </div>
                  {% endfor %}
                </div>
              {% else %}
                <p class="ff-gil-shop-empty">No missing marketboard purchases found.</p>
              {% endif %}
            </details>
          </article>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      <div class="ff-gil-shopping-footnotes">
        <p>{{ s.notes.vendor }}</p>
        <p>{{ s.notes.market }}</p>
        <p>{{ s.notes.ownership }}</p>
        <p>{{ s.notes.orchestrions }}</p>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <section class="ff-gil-afford ff-card">
    <div class="ff-gil-section-head ff-gil-section-head--compact">
      <div>
        <p class="ff-gil-kicker">◇ what can I spend?</p>
        <h2>The anti-impulse-purchase box</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ff-gil-afford-grid">
      <article>
        <small>Current floor</small>
        <strong>{{ g.gilFloorDisplay }}</strong>
        <p>The amount I’m pretending does not exist.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <small>Safe spending pot</small>
        <strong>{{ g.safeSpendDisplay }}</strong>
        <p>Anything above the floor is fair game for collection nonsense.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <small>Next savings flag</small>
        <strong>{{ g.nextMilestone.display }}</strong>
        <p>
          {% if g.currentGil > 0 %}
            {{ g.nextMilestone.deltaDisplay }} away.
          {% else %}
            Add current gil and this starts calculating itself.
          {% endif %}
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="ff-gil-rulebook">
      <span aria-hidden="true">♡</span>
      <p>
        <strong>Frog Treasury rule:</strong>
        hit milestones, raise the safety floor over time, and let expensive
        collection purchases become part of the story instead of treating every
        purchase like lost progress.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ff-gil-diary ff-card">
    <div class="ff-gil-section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="ff-gil-kicker">✧ purchase diary</p>
        <h2>Things I spent an upsetting amount of gil on</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Add purchases to <code>purchaseDiary</code> in the data file and they
        automatically feed Collector Spending + Lifetime Progress.
      </p>
    </div>

    {% if g.purchases.length %}
      <div class="ff-gil-diary-list">
        {% for purchase in g.purchases %}
          <article>
            <div class="ff-gil-diary__mark" aria-hidden="true">◇</div>
            <div>
              <small>{{ purchase.type or "Collectible" }}{% if purchase.date %} · {{ purchase.date }}{% endif %}</small>
              <strong>{{ purchase.name }}</strong>
              {% if purchase.note %}<p>{{ purchase.note }}</p>{% endif %}
            </div>
            <span>{{ purchase.costDisplay }}</span>
          </article>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    {% else %}
      <div class="ff-gil-diary-empty">
        <span aria-hidden="true">◇</span>
        <strong>No ridiculous purchases logged yet.</strong>
        <p>Enjoy this brief and probably temporary period of financial responsibility.</p>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <section class="ff-gil-endgame ff-card">
    <span class="ff-gil-endgame__crown" aria-hidden="true">♛</span>
    <p class="ff-gil-kicker">final boss</p>
    <h2>{{ g.capDisplay }}</h2>
    <p>
      Not a sensible target. Not a quick target. Just the eventual end of the
      Frog Treasury road.
    </p>
    <div class="ff-gil-endgame__sparkles" aria-hidden="true">✦　◇　♡　◇　✦</div>
  </section>
</div>


<script>
  (() => {
    const input = document.querySelector("[data-gil-shopping-search]");
    if (!input) return;

    const rows = [...document.querySelectorAll("[data-gil-shopping-row]")];

    input.addEventListener("input", () => {
      const query = input.value.trim().toLowerCase();

      rows.forEach((row) => {
        const name = row.dataset.gilShoppingName || "";
        row.hidden = Boolean(query) && !name.includes(query);
      });
    });
  })();
</script>
